### The 16 bugs fixed (file:line → fix)
1. **`BattleDirector.cs` `End()`** — shootdodge time-scale key never cleared if battle ends while
   airborne (permanent slow-mo softlock). Fixed: `End()` now clears `ShootdodgeKey` and resets
   `_wasShootdodging`.
2. **`BattleDirector.cs` `CheckOutcome()`** — Defeat didn't guard against racing an in-flight
   `Executing` action coroutine (Victory already did). Fixed: added `&& Phase != BattlePhase.Executing`
   to the Defeat branch, mirroring Victory.
3. **`Door.cs` `Transition()`** — unguarded null-deref on `_destination` mid-fade, could freeze the
   player behind a permanent black screen. Fixed: early null-check + `Debug.LogError` in `Interact()`
   before anything starts.
4. **`Door.cs`** — coroutine not stopped on disable, `_busy`/player-lock could get stuck. Fixed:
   added `OnDisable()` that unlocks a tracked `_transitioningPlayer`, resets fade, clears `_busy`.
5. **`Gate.cs`** — same coroutine-not-stopped pattern. Fixed: added `OnDisable()` resetting `_busy`.
6. **`Gate.cs` `Interact()`/`Swing()`** — key consumed immediately but `_unlocked` only set ~0.6s
   later at the end of the swing animation (desync window: a save/state-read mid-swing sees
   `Locked == true` with the key already gone). Fixed: moved `_unlocked = true` to right after key
   consumption in `Interact()`, matching `Door.cs`'s pattern; removed it from the end of `Swing()`.
7. **`Container.cs` `InteractStage()`** — a guaranteed/fixed item (e.g. a quest key) was silently
   lost forever if the bag was full on first search (unlike `Pickup.cs`, which keeps itself alive
   for overflow). Fixed: added `_pendingFixed` list; fixed items that don't fit are re-offered on
   later search stages/sessions instead of being dropped, bounded by `_stage < MaxStages` so it can
   never infinite-loop in `Interact()`'s `while (InteractStage(player))`.
8. **`SaveSystem.cs` `Save()`** — non-atomic `File.WriteAllText` straight over the live save file;
   a crash mid-write truncates it, silently losing the whole save on next load. Fixed: write to a
   `.tmp` file then `File.Replace`/`File.Move` it into place atomically.
9. **`SaveGame.cs` `IsValid`** — didn't check list fields (`Bag`, `Weapons`, `Facts`, etc.) for null;
   a corrupted/hand-edited save with e.g. `"Bag": null` passed validation then threw an unhandled
   NRE mid-restore in `SaveSystem.ApplyPending()`. Fixed: `IsValid` now also requires all 8 list
   fields to be non-null.
10. **`Autopilot.cs` `WaitForReload()`** — unhandled NRE if the 20s reload-wait deadline passed
    while `GameSession.Instance` was still null. Fixed: added a null-check after the wait loop that
    logs `FAIL`, increments `_failures`, and returns cleanly instead of crashing.
11. **`EnemyActor.cs` `TakeHit()`** — invented a whole stagger/poise rule (magic numbers `20`, `0.35`,
    `1.8`) directly in a MonoBehaviour, violating the project's "Presentation never decides a rule"
    law. Fixed: extracted to a new pure `UnityEve.Core.Battle.StaggerRule.ShouldStagger(recentDamage,
    maxHp)` + 3 new `BattleConfig` constants (`StaggerDamageFloor`, `StaggerDamageFraction`,
    `StaggerStunSeconds`); added 2 unit tests in `BattleRulesTests.cs`.
12. **`BattleDirector.Commands.cs` `OpenCommandMenu()`** — didn't itself guard against an open Focus
    window (only the `Update()` call site did); `Autopilot.cs` calls it directly, bypassing that
    check. Fixed: added `|| _focus.IsOpen` to the early-return guard.
13. **`DemoContentBuilder.Characters.cs` `CreatureAnimator()`** — reintroduced the exact
    clip-orphaning bug already fixed for the player rig (`OwnedClip` deletes+recreates the `.anim`
    asset every call, no de-dup) for every non-player creature; a Walk/Run clip-name collision
    silently loses the Walk motion in the saved `.controller`. Fixed: added the same `owned`
    memoization dictionary `PlayerAnimator()` already uses.
14. **`Autopilot.cs` `SetupOffscreen()`** — leaked a `RenderTexture` + `PanelSettings` instance every
    call (happens ≥2x per standard autoplay run, every lap forever in `-demo`). Fixed: added a
    `_panel` field; releases/destroys the previous `_offscreen`/`_panel` before making new ones,
    mirroring `GameHud.EnsureTarget()`.
15. **`ItemDatabase.cs` `Find()`** — cache invalidation keyed only on `_byId.Count != Items.Count`:
    an in-place swap at the same index never changes count (stale lookup survives); a duplicate-id
    authoring mistake collapses the dict below `Items.Count` forever (full rebuild every call).
    Fixed: removed the count heuristic; cache now builds once lazily (`_byId == null`) and an
    `OnValidate()` clears it on editor/inspector edits.
16. **`LootTable.cs` `RollOne()`** — a zero/negative-weight entry wasn't properly skipped at the
    exact `pick == 0f` boundary (an entry with `Weight <= 0` could still be returned if
    `rng.NextFloat()` drew exactly `0`). Fixed: explicit `if (weight <= 0f) continue;` before the
    `pick -=` subtraction, so a disabled-weight entry can never match regardless of the boundary.

**Not fixed (flagged, left as-is):**
- `ScreenEncounters.cs:75-76` event subscriptions (`CameraDirector.ZoneChanged`,
  `BattleDirector.BattleEnded`) never unsubscribed in `OnDestroy()`. Low risk, same pattern exists
  elsewhere unflagged; recommended against fixing, user didn't push back.

